          "reason": "The conditioned-survival theorem explicitly applies the generic path-overlap chain rule to its conditioned ordinary-state kernels. Taking l=0 and substituting T_M,surv into the canonical formula gives exactly the removed conditioned full-path product. The theorem retains positive initial survival, normalized conditional path laws, the joint-positive denominator condition for the geometric-mean kernel, and arbitrary completion of unreachable zero-survival rows. The old conditioned result is therefore a stated specialization of the generic equation; its additional normalization/survival proof remains at ptnb:thm:conditioned-survival, rather than being attributed to the generic path-product declaration.",
